Review dimensional models and the evidence for a design decision (@engineering-geometric-review: 0, is #chapter, #hephaestus-core "Define-the-boundary-ports-and-stored-quantities-before-a-balance.lingua#r_007A17F7243A9F54EDDD173BA3") { r_014ED719C2EE20565F21353AD0
Explain the tray study to someone who has only the requirement and your drawing. Reconstruct the intended ideal geometry, define the gap, identify the independent dimensions and distinguish a label from evidence about a real object. Reuse [Review engineering claims from function to continuing service](Review-engineering-claims-from-function-to-continuing-service.lingua#r_0226B0839C667959908DA37D5B) for the common function-to-service questions; this block deepens their quantitative geometrical application rather than completing an engineering discipline.

**Demonstrate:** distinguish a perspective sketch, coordinate view, section, schematic, part description and assembly description. Identify projection directions, units and reference conditions. Recover a missing coordinate from matched views and give an example where a single view loses information. Show why a rotation/translation preserves distance while numerical coordinate differences can change direction or sign.

**Derive:** state the assembly closure and its assumptions, expose a redundant or inconsistent dimension, propagate signed bounds, and distinguish possible success from guaranteed success within the model. Prove the affine endpoint bound. Preserve shared input dependence before taking intervals. Derive an example where a common effect cancels and another where it does not. Explain why an interval alone supplies neither a production distribution nor a yield estimate.

**Decide from evidence:** separate allowed dimensional limits, a measured estimate, uncertainty and a decision rule. Use the inclusive endpoint cases to defend within/outside/unresolved conclusions under the stipulated hard-bound model. Explain why that model is different from probabilistic measurement uncertainty and why a historical guide is not a declaration of current compliance. Identify geometrical features that the chosen procedure cannot observe and the consequences for the engineering claim.

**Independent work:** choose another benign fit, such as a paper layout inside a frame, and derive its own model rather than reusing the tray numbers. Write two candidate designs, reject one by an explicit constraint, and state the evidence needed to compare the remainder. Preserve intermediate calculations and one correction made after criticism. Mathematical consistency alone does not establish material behavior, manufacturing capability or continuing usefulness.

Read the assigned shared drawing and measurement sources progressively. Return to [Solve simultaneous constraints without losing their solution set](../../mathematics/core/Solve-simultaneous-constraints-without-losing-their-solution-set.lingua#r_03FC1F97250326F9B36A1B2F6B), [Distinguish a point a displacement and its coordinates](../../mathematics/core/Distinguish-a-point-a-displacement-and-its-coordinates.lingua#r_062423188E960EBAB9A92CE3E4), [Interpret equilibrium solutions through support constraints and evidence](../../physics/core/Interpret-equilibrium-solutions-through-support-constraints-and-evidence.lingua#r_08587ABAC04444B08A9A548CFC) and [Compare alternatives under constraints and explicit tradeoffs](Compare-alternatives-under-constraints-and-explicit-tradeoffs.lingua#r_0848D9CBAED01BC33DD0081EA7) when a conclusion depends on their preparation. Later engineering formation still includes material and structural response, circuits and transport, realization, control, reliability, human use, environmental accounts and advanced practical/academic work. The next common block develops inquiry's design, dependence and finite-chance reasoning before specialized engineering extensions.

**Next common area:** [review the first inquiry block](../../inquiry/core/Review-the-chain-from-question-to-shared-scientific-claim.lingua#r_0093C5B9C7363BE10B1DFAD7E5), then develop study design, dependence and finite-chance reasoning at comparable depth.

**Return:** [Engineering](../Engineering.lingua#r_5DA6VY09MAD2N8D9SH0FFJVV68).

**Continue in the third common pass:** [Define the boundary ports and stored quantities before a balance](Define-the-boundary-ports-and-stored-quantities-before-a-balance.lingua#r_007A17F7243A9F54EDDD173BA3). Comparable mathematics, physics, chemistry and computing blocks now supply preparation; the earlier service and assembly studies remain unchanged.

